WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:01.086
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.086 --> 00:00:03.419
- What's up Andrew?
- What's up Steven?

00:00:03.419 --> 00:00:06.252
- I made you a letter.
- Worth it brunch.

00:00:06.252 --> 00:00:07.448
Will you go to brunch with me?

00:00:07.448 --> 00:00:08.281
Circle.

00:00:09.538 --> 00:00:11.205
How about this?
- No.

00:00:12.208 --> 00:00:13.517
- Yeah I'll go to brunch with you.

00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:16.640
- Okay, I spent like 20 minutes on that.

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.005
You didn't even--
- Waste of time, not worth it.

00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:20.921
- Tell me about brunch.

00:00:20.921 --> 00:00:21.881
- I'll tell you about brunch.

00:00:21.881 --> 00:00:23.181
Brunch is dumb.

00:00:23.181 --> 00:00:24.586
- Brunch is not dumb.

00:00:24.586 --> 00:00:25.805
Brunch is an event.

00:00:25.805 --> 00:00:29.439
It's a place where you can
extend breakfast into lunch

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:31.274
and create a new memory.

00:00:31.274 --> 00:00:33.468
A memory that we shall call brunch.

00:00:33.468 --> 00:00:36.022
Today on Worth It we're going
to be trying three brunches

00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:38.112
at three drastically different
price points to find out

00:00:38.112 --> 00:00:40.829
which one is the most
worth it at its price.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:43.104
And actually, we're doing the
brunch across three Sundays.

00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:45.496
Triple the fun, triple the action--

00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:47.237
- Prolonging the pain.

00:00:47.237 --> 00:00:49.397
- He says that, but he truly loves me.

00:00:49.397 --> 00:00:50.802
- So the first place we're going to

00:00:50.802 --> 00:00:52.936
is in fact not a brunch place.

00:00:52.936 --> 00:00:54.714
- Yes, they serve breakfast, but

00:00:54.714 --> 00:00:57.300
they serve it from
eight a.m. to three p.m.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.631
So, what do you do when you
need breakfast at three p.m.?

00:00:59.631 --> 00:01:02.136
- Isn't that a combination
of breakfast and dinner?

00:01:02.136 --> 00:01:02.969
- What? (scoffs)

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:03.810
Where are you going here?

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:04.643
- Brinner?

00:01:04.643 --> 00:01:05.476
Brupper?

00:01:05.476 --> 00:01:07.542
(laughing)

00:01:07.542 --> 00:01:10.631
(banjo music)

00:01:10.631 --> 00:01:11.464
- I'm Brianna.

00:01:11.464 --> 00:01:12.297
You can call me Breezy.

00:01:12.297 --> 00:01:13.471
I'm the owner founder of Homestate.

00:01:13.471 --> 00:01:15.282
And today we're going to
be eating breakfast tacos.

00:01:15.282 --> 00:01:16.730
- When you started Homestate, did you

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:20.097
initially see it as a
breakfast taco primarily?

00:01:20.097 --> 00:01:22.011
- Yes (laughs) and queso.

00:01:22.011 --> 00:01:24.846
My mission in life was to serve
breakfast tacos and queso,

00:01:24.846 --> 00:01:26.831
because no one else in
L.A. was doing that.

00:01:26.831 --> 00:01:28.271
I was like, "This is crazy!"

00:01:28.271 --> 00:01:29.907
We opened with really bad queso.

00:01:29.907 --> 00:01:31.510
I thought we were going
to go down because,

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:32.717
like, you know, it's a big deal.

00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:35.050
We finally got it about
a year after we opened.

00:01:35.050 --> 00:01:37.025
- So what is your secret?
- It's real cheese.

00:01:37.025 --> 00:01:41.204
Blended with jalapenos,
serranos, onions, tomatoes.

00:01:41.204 --> 00:01:43.805
It's a huge part of your
breakfast taco experience.

00:01:43.805 --> 00:01:44.638
- [Andrew] Really?

00:01:44.638 --> 00:01:45.877
- [Brianna] Because you
need to dip the taco--

00:01:45.877 --> 00:01:48.162
- Oh.
- In the queso.

00:01:48.162 --> 00:01:50.321
It will take your dining
experience from here

00:01:50.321 --> 00:01:51.819
to like (whooshing).

00:01:51.819 --> 00:01:53.485
You have to do the Trinity.

00:01:53.485 --> 00:01:56.370
By a country mile, like our
most favorite loved taco.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.619
It's on a flour tortilla, flour
tortilla is king in Texas.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.160
We make the tortillas by hand.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.645
They're made fresh to order.

00:02:02.645 --> 00:02:05.839
We have scrambled eggs, which
are really beautifully cooked.

00:02:05.839 --> 00:02:08.776
Topped with crispy potatoes, crispy bacon,

00:02:08.776 --> 00:02:10.773
and melted cheddar cheese.

00:02:10.773 --> 00:02:11.679
- [Andrew] I like that we're having coffee

00:02:11.679 --> 00:02:13.498
as the first beverage that
we have in this episode,

00:02:13.498 --> 00:02:16.215
because brunch is nothing but breakfast.

00:02:16.215 --> 00:02:17.933
- See, this is why you're on this trip.

00:02:17.933 --> 00:02:19.594
We need to educate you.

00:02:19.594 --> 00:02:20.427
Cheers.

00:02:21.633 --> 00:02:23.129
- Start with the Trinity?
- Let's go.

00:02:23.129 --> 00:02:25.521
- The tortilla smells incredible.

00:02:25.521 --> 00:02:26.833
It's like a baby's thigh.

00:02:26.833 --> 00:02:28.500
So soft and squishy.

00:02:29.631 --> 00:02:30.464
In a good way!

00:02:30.464 --> 00:02:31.297
In a good way.

00:02:31.297 --> 00:02:32.130
- Okay, okay.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:32.963
Cheers.

00:02:34.847 --> 00:02:36.415
Wow
- That's so good.

00:02:36.415 --> 00:02:38.449
- That, oh
- It is, at face value

00:02:38.449 --> 00:02:41.096
pretty basic breakfast components,

00:02:41.096 --> 00:02:44.138
but with the tortilla, it's so much more.

00:02:44.138 --> 00:02:45.612
- The egg is the game changer here.

00:02:45.612 --> 00:02:48.039
It fills your mouth with
the thing that egg does,

00:02:48.039 --> 00:02:51.057
which tastes good, and is fluffy.

00:02:51.057 --> 00:02:52.140
Oh
- Aww man.

00:02:54.322 --> 00:02:55.285
- This Is Amazing.

00:02:55.285 --> 00:02:56.525
- This combination?

00:02:56.525 --> 00:02:57.514
Luscious.

00:02:57.514 --> 00:02:59.024
- [Brianna] We're also going
to do the vegetarian taco.

00:02:59.024 --> 00:03:02.298
When I was living in Texas I
was vegetarian for 12 years.

00:03:02.298 --> 00:03:04.968
For me, the vegetarian
taco was pretty critical.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.708
It sounds like a boring
taco until you try it.

00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:09.658
But it's the Blanco, it's egg whites with

00:03:09.658 --> 00:03:12.908
shiitake mushrooms and Monterey cheese.

00:03:14.987 --> 00:03:15.820
- Ohh...

00:03:18.621 --> 00:03:21.094
I love this taco as much as I love you.

00:03:21.094 --> 00:03:22.197
- Wish I could say the same.

00:03:22.197 --> 00:03:25.007
- Is it because you love me so
much that it doesn't compare?

00:03:25.007 --> 00:03:25.840
That's what I'm hearing.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:29.430
- Mushroom is as powerful
a flavor as any meat.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.742
- Vegetarian friends, sometimes

00:03:30.742 --> 00:03:31.983
you guys get the short end of the stick.

00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:33.598
You can't eat brisket,
you can't eat bacon,

00:03:33.598 --> 00:03:35.442
but it's okay, because
they have designed this

00:03:35.442 --> 00:03:37.496
beautiful, simple taco just for you.

00:03:37.496 --> 00:03:38.471
- [Brianna] The final taco is the Pecos,

00:03:38.471 --> 00:03:41.037
which is another favorite and
that's also really simple.

00:03:41.037 --> 00:03:43.080
It's just scrambled eggs
and shredded brisket.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.054
The brisket is cooked over 12 hours.

00:03:45.054 --> 00:03:47.585
We do nothing to it but
put salt and pepper on it.

00:03:47.585 --> 00:03:48.418
- [Andrew] Really?

00:03:48.418 --> 00:03:49.556
- [Brianna] It's just a
really good quality beef.

00:03:49.556 --> 00:03:51.045
- Nice and slow.
- Yeah, nice and--

00:03:51.045 --> 00:03:52.066
- Love it.
- Slow and low.

00:03:52.066 --> 00:03:53.576
- Yeah
- That sounds awesome.

00:03:53.576 --> 00:03:54.954
- What more do you need in life

00:03:54.954 --> 00:03:57.961
than egg, brisket, and flour tortillas?

00:03:57.961 --> 00:03:59.794
- Cheese on top maybe?

00:04:01.293 --> 00:04:03.876
(upbeat music)

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.978
You know, I do have to stand
a little bit corrected.

00:04:06.978 --> 00:04:08.478
This is way more than breakfast.

00:04:08.478 --> 00:04:10.742
I'm eating slow roasted brisket--

00:04:10.742 --> 00:04:12.019
- Can we talk about the brisket?

00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:13.703
- Can you talk about
the tortillas some more?

00:04:13.703 --> 00:04:14.817
- Can we talk about the egg?

00:04:14.817 --> 00:04:17.171
- It's perfect with just a
little bit of sauce on that.

00:04:17.171 --> 00:04:20.921
- Oh, thank you, that's
what best friends do.

00:04:22.132 --> 00:04:23.965
Here you go my friend.

00:04:26.335 --> 00:04:30.502
Has anybody ever told you that
you take really large bites?

00:04:32.152 --> 00:04:32.985
(laughs)

00:04:32.985 --> 00:04:34.700
- Oh God!
- What'd you think?

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.608
- We did that wrong.

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:37.242
We should have got two tacos each.

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:39.367
- But that's why you eat brunch at,

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:40.804
you know, 11 a.m. then you've got

00:04:40.804 --> 00:04:43.243
the rest of Sunday to just nap.

00:04:43.243 --> 00:04:44.076
Brunch and nap.

00:04:44.076 --> 00:04:45.215
Brunch fact!

00:04:45.215 --> 00:04:47.455
Brunch is speculated to come from

00:04:47.455 --> 00:04:49.543
men who used to hunt in the U.K.

00:04:49.543 --> 00:04:50.625
They would need to get their nourishment

00:04:50.625 --> 00:04:52.007
so they would eat breakfast and lunch

00:04:52.007 --> 00:04:55.198
combined into one large
meal, with an adult beverage.

00:04:55.198 --> 00:04:56.639
- Adult beverage and hunting?

00:04:56.639 --> 00:04:57.925
Sounds like my kind of day.

00:04:57.925 --> 00:04:59.667
- Alright Governors, let's go hunting.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.025
- Ugh, I haven't eaten yet.

00:05:01.025 --> 00:05:02.801
Shall we combine breakfast and lunch?

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:03.634
That's nonsense.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:04.891
Let's call it brunch.

00:05:04.891 --> 00:05:06.259
- Sounds way better.

00:05:06.259 --> 00:05:08.149
- Can I enjoy an adult beverage during?

00:05:08.149 --> 00:05:09.927
I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:05:09.927 --> 00:05:10.760
- So we're done for today.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.362
It's time for our little nap.

00:05:12.362 --> 00:05:14.336
Next week we're going to A-Frame.

00:05:14.336 --> 00:05:15.729
- And what do they do there?

00:05:15.729 --> 00:05:17.769
- Stacks on stacks on stacks
on stacks on stacks on--

00:05:17.769 --> 00:05:20.352
(upbeat music)

00:05:21.328 --> 00:05:22.471
- Alright, my name is Roy.

00:05:22.471 --> 00:05:23.304
Welcome to A-Frame.

00:05:23.304 --> 00:05:25.248
We serve pancakes on the
weekend, all you can eat.

00:05:25.248 --> 00:05:26.763
If you look around, this is an old IHOP,

00:05:26.763 --> 00:05:28.573
so it makes sense to
serve pancakes in here.

00:05:28.573 --> 00:05:30.002
We gutted this whole
thing out and we saw these

00:05:30.002 --> 00:05:31.361
beautiful beams and everything.

00:05:31.361 --> 00:05:33.299
Right at the time we were creating A-Frame

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.554
I was going to Hawaii a lot.

00:05:34.554 --> 00:05:36.539
So, I was like, channeling
the spirit of the island.

00:05:36.539 --> 00:05:38.942
We were serving Korean
Hawaiian inspired food.

00:05:38.942 --> 00:05:40.833
For the first two years
this was that restaurant.

00:05:40.833 --> 00:05:42.309
And then we decided to open for brunch.

00:05:42.309 --> 00:05:43.958
Personally and professionally you avoid

00:05:43.958 --> 00:05:45.095
what's right in front of you.

00:05:45.095 --> 00:05:47.046
Finally confronted, you know what?

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:47.879
Ding.
(laughs)

00:05:47.879 --> 00:05:48.712
We're an IHOP.

00:05:48.712 --> 00:05:50.053
We made it an all you can eat brunch.

00:05:50.053 --> 00:05:53.870
I like to use a really strong,
stable, buttermilk recipe.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.600
Just straight up classic, your grandma

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:57.121
wouldn't be mad type of pancake.

00:05:57.121 --> 00:05:58.828
And then from there, we add toppings.

00:05:58.828 --> 00:06:00.755
You get two pancakes per order, per stack

00:06:00.755 --> 00:06:02.171
and all you have to do is raise your hand

00:06:02.171 --> 00:06:03.645
and it just keeps getting filled up.

00:06:03.645 --> 00:06:05.885
- [Andrew] Why also bottomless drinks?

00:06:05.885 --> 00:06:07.044
- [Roy] Now, we tried to think of like,

00:06:07.044 --> 00:06:09.471
how can I make places
that everyone can access?

00:06:09.471 --> 00:06:11.595
So that's what the all you can drink is.

00:06:11.595 --> 00:06:13.999
We have a michelada,
it's like a spicy beer.

00:06:13.999 --> 00:06:16.251
It's like a Bloody Mary
and a beer had sex.

00:06:16.251 --> 00:06:19.305
A Dos Equis Lager, a
mimosa, and a bloody Mary.

00:06:19.305 --> 00:06:20.138
- Cheers.

00:06:20.976 --> 00:06:22.143
Mmm.
- Oh yeah.

00:06:23.025 --> 00:06:24.093
- I'm going to eat more than you today.

00:06:24.093 --> 00:06:24.926
- Ha!
- Ha!

00:06:24.926 --> 00:06:25.759
(laughing)

00:06:25.759 --> 00:06:26.592
You ate breakfast.

00:06:26.592 --> 00:06:27.425
You made a mistake.

00:06:27.425 --> 00:06:28.815
- That's called priming your stomach.

00:06:28.815 --> 00:06:30.534
- Alright, let's- pancake number one.

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:31.764
- [Roy] Right off the griddle, hot,

00:06:31.764 --> 00:06:33.709
we lather them with a lilikoi butter.

00:06:33.709 --> 00:06:34.975
This is a passion fruit butter

00:06:34.975 --> 00:06:37.017
that we make into compound butter.

00:06:37.017 --> 00:06:38.060
- Excited for this one,
because it's sweet.

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:39.524
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:06:39.524 --> 00:06:41.126
You're going double dog.
- Yeah.

00:06:41.126 --> 00:06:42.933
When you eat a stack of pancakes

00:06:42.933 --> 00:06:44.710
you eat the whole stack at once.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.709
- Uh uh.
- Really?

00:06:45.709 --> 00:06:46.635
- Yes!
- You separate pancake--

00:06:46.635 --> 00:06:47.468
- You eat the first one.
- No!

00:06:47.468 --> 00:06:48.797
- Alright, I'll do your style.

00:06:48.797 --> 00:06:49.630
Cheers.

00:06:51.885 --> 00:06:52.860
This is going to be a great day.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.008
Excuse me while I eat more.

00:06:54.008 --> 00:06:56.576
Woo, nuts, on pancakes.
(laughs)

00:06:56.576 --> 00:06:58.464
Texture of that together--
- Is that a great combination?

00:06:58.464 --> 00:06:59.297
- Yeah
- Yeah.

00:06:59.297 --> 00:07:00.130
- It's fluffy and nutty.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:01.694
- Yeah. I'm fluffy--
- Ever have a fluffer-nutter?

00:07:01.694 --> 00:07:02.527
- You're nutty.

00:07:02.527 --> 00:07:03.806
- Actually could use
a little syrup for me.

00:07:03.806 --> 00:07:05.711
- No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:07:05.711 --> 00:07:06.544
- Oh yeah.
- Syrup's too rich.

00:07:06.544 --> 00:07:07.754
- No.
- I'm a purist.

00:07:07.754 --> 00:07:09.345
Pancake number one down.

00:07:09.345 --> 00:07:10.251
Let's go for the next one.

00:07:10.251 --> 00:07:12.130
- [Roy] We have the banana
macadamia nut butter.

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:14.767
We make a macadamia nut pesto with banana.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.727
Then we serve that with whipped cream.

00:07:16.727 --> 00:07:19.074
- [Steven] Banana macadamia nut.

00:07:19.074 --> 00:07:21.164
- Macadamian.
- Macadanian?

00:07:21.164 --> 00:07:23.326
- Macadamian?
- Macadamia.

00:07:23.326 --> 00:07:24.243
- Alright.
- This is fun.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.897
We're having fun at brunch, let's eat.

00:07:25.897 --> 00:07:28.323
- So banana, oh, excuse me.
(laughs)

00:07:28.323 --> 00:07:30.854
Banana and pancake is
the classic combo for me.

00:07:30.854 --> 00:07:34.543
A soft fluffy texture
with a soft mushy texture

00:07:34.543 --> 00:07:35.731
that goes so well together.

00:07:35.731 --> 00:07:37.281
- We need a Wimpy bite.

00:07:37.281 --> 00:07:38.114
Cheers.

00:07:39.197 --> 00:07:40.030
The thing you just said about,

00:07:40.030 --> 00:07:42.191
you know mushy and soft together?

00:07:42.191 --> 00:07:44.164
That's what's happening
in my mouth just now.

00:07:44.164 --> 00:07:45.919
- [Roy] Then we have the
pineapple orange guava,

00:07:45.919 --> 00:07:47.382
which is, almost like a jam.

00:07:47.382 --> 00:07:49.382
- Can I feed you a bite?

00:07:51.872 --> 00:07:52.766
Let me know what you think about that.

00:07:52.766 --> 00:07:54.136
It's not quite like the others.

00:07:54.136 --> 00:07:55.878
It's a little more tart and

00:07:55.878 --> 00:07:58.548
it's got that pineapple acidity to it.

00:07:58.548 --> 00:08:00.939
- Feels like I'm on Hawaii,
like lying in the sand.

00:08:00.939 --> 00:08:02.577
The world is passing by me.

00:08:02.577 --> 00:08:04.666
- And suddenly some fruit
falls from a tree and lands

00:08:04.666 --> 00:08:07.162
in your mouth, right?
- Yeah.

00:08:07.162 --> 00:08:08.660
- [Roy] And then we have
the buttermilk chicken.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:10.342
Which is our buttermilk pancake with a

00:08:10.342 --> 00:08:12.608
mochiko rice flour fried chicken.

00:08:12.608 --> 00:08:14.871
Kind of Japanese style,
Japanese Hawaiian style.

00:08:14.871 --> 00:08:17.419
- Woo!
- Now I kinda feel like

00:08:17.419 --> 00:08:18.975
we've finally arrived at brunch.

00:08:18.975 --> 00:08:20.050
- You're a smart guy Andrew.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:21.107
That's why I bring you on these.

00:08:21.107 --> 00:08:21.940
- Thank you.

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.409
- You're so charming and smart and

00:08:24.409 --> 00:08:27.787
what a great--
- I'm gonna eat it.

00:08:27.787 --> 00:08:28.925
- This is the way to do it.
- Yeah.

00:08:28.925 --> 00:08:30.237
- Start with the sweeter ones.

00:08:30.237 --> 00:08:33.590
Then when lunch comes
around, 11 a.m., 12 p.m.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.926
you go to the chicken.
- The rest of the lunch hours?

00:08:35.926 --> 00:08:36.846
This is the first time we've had

00:08:36.846 --> 00:08:38.376
the buttermilk pancake on its own.

00:08:38.376 --> 00:08:39.209
It's beautiful.

00:08:39.209 --> 00:08:40.059
- Did you eat it with fried chicken?

00:08:40.059 --> 00:08:42.495
- I didn't have it together.
- You made the mistake.

00:08:42.495 --> 00:08:43.328
- Do it.
- Here.

00:08:43.328 --> 00:08:44.161
I'll give you some of mine.

00:08:44.161 --> 00:08:46.624
You have the fried chicken
off a fluffy pancake.

00:08:46.624 --> 00:08:49.134
The dynamic duo of friendship.

00:08:49.134 --> 00:08:51.385
- I think we have a
special treat for Adam.

00:08:51.385 --> 00:08:54.218
(uplifting music)

00:09:06.177 --> 00:09:08.032
- [Steven] Matt, thanks for driving.

00:09:08.032 --> 00:09:08.865
- [Steven] Appreciate it.

00:09:08.865 --> 00:09:10.838
Allowed me to enjoy a drink on the show.

00:09:10.838 --> 00:09:13.044
What'd you think?
- What did you think?

00:09:13.044 --> 00:09:14.078
- Dude, that was so good.

00:09:14.078 --> 00:09:16.597
Unlimited pancakes.
- Yeah.

00:09:16.597 --> 00:09:17.628
- Come on.

00:09:17.628 --> 00:09:18.461
Come on!

00:09:18.461 --> 00:09:20.378
Pancakes are delicious.

00:09:22.251 --> 00:09:23.191
Brunch Fact!

00:09:23.191 --> 00:09:25.699
Dude, I have to pee so bad.

00:09:25.699 --> 00:09:26.532
- That's not a brunch fact.

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.427
- Those mimosas in water glasses.

00:09:28.427 --> 00:09:29.260
(laughs)

00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:30.768
- If I tickle you, will you pee?

00:09:30.768 --> 00:09:31.638
- Brunch fact!

00:09:31.638 --> 00:09:34.924
Brunch was popularized in
America most likely because,

00:09:34.924 --> 00:09:36.457
as actors were traveling from the

00:09:36.457 --> 00:09:37.374
east coast to the west coast,

00:09:37.374 --> 00:09:40.903
they would stop by Chicago
for a mid-morning meal.

00:09:40.903 --> 00:09:42.691
Planes couldn't fly, you know,
all the way across the coast.

00:09:42.691 --> 00:09:44.224
So they would stop in
the middle of the country

00:09:44.224 --> 00:09:45.974
and then finish the flight at the end.

00:09:45.974 --> 00:09:47.448
- Wow, that melted my brain.

00:09:47.448 --> 00:09:48.772
- Melted your brain?

00:09:48.772 --> 00:09:50.722
- Melted it like butter on a pancake.

00:09:50.722 --> 00:09:52.080
- So we've had breakfast tacos.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.578
We've had all you can eat pancakes.

00:09:53.578 --> 00:09:57.050
And finally, we're on
the way to the last spot.

00:09:57.050 --> 00:09:58.361
- Next week--
- I'll see you next week.

00:09:58.361 --> 00:09:59.546
- The ultimate brunch.

00:09:59.546 --> 00:10:02.295
- Seafood, champagne, no caviar.

00:10:02.295 --> 00:10:04.878
(upbeat music)

00:10:07.197 --> 00:10:08.461
- My name is David Codney,
I'm the executive chef

00:10:08.461 --> 00:10:09.762
of the Peninsula Beverly Hills

00:10:09.762 --> 00:10:11.794
and you are here to dine with
us for our Sunday brunch.

00:10:11.794 --> 00:10:12.906
We like to do things that are just fun,

00:10:12.906 --> 00:10:13.753
a little bit different.

00:10:13.753 --> 00:10:16.191
More of the old school nod at
to how brunches used to be.

00:10:16.191 --> 00:10:17.248
It's done with a modern twist.

00:10:17.248 --> 00:10:18.699
You know, we like things
where it's slower paced,

00:10:18.699 --> 00:10:20.174
people can walk through at their leisure.

00:10:20.174 --> 00:10:21.869
Hence, the champagne, so you can just

00:10:21.869 --> 00:10:22.821
sit there and have fun.

00:10:22.821 --> 00:10:23.749
And if you don't like your family,

00:10:23.749 --> 00:10:24.922
you can always drink a little bit more.

00:10:24.922 --> 00:10:26.478
- I think brunch is
like the ultimate way to

00:10:26.478 --> 00:10:27.720
like, win somebody's heart, right?

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:28.997
- I would agree.

00:10:28.997 --> 00:10:30.530
First dates, family time.

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:31.911
And when it gets awkward,
you just eat more.

00:10:31.911 --> 00:10:33.177
We feature, for our Sunday brunch,

00:10:33.177 --> 00:10:34.709
many, many, many, different items.

00:10:34.709 --> 00:10:36.822
We have jumbo shrimp cocktail, oysters,

00:10:36.822 --> 00:10:38.459
snow crab claws, Peruvian based

00:10:38.459 --> 00:10:40.235
scallop ceviche, house smoked salmon.

00:10:40.235 --> 00:10:43.034
We do a taramasalata, which
is a Greek cod roe dip.

00:10:43.034 --> 00:10:45.412
We also have braised pork
belly, lamb pastrami.

00:10:45.412 --> 00:10:47.594
It's usually done with a brisket,
but we use a leg of lamb.

00:10:47.594 --> 00:10:49.431
So we cure it and brine it for three days,

00:10:49.431 --> 00:10:50.776
and then we smoke it for 4 hours,

00:10:50.776 --> 00:10:52.333
and then slowly roast it overnight.

00:10:52.333 --> 00:10:54.794
- [Andrew] Lamb pastrami, that's
not a typical thing, right?

00:10:54.794 --> 00:10:56.523
- No, it's a little twist,
everything's a twist.

00:10:56.523 --> 00:10:57.964
The lobster waffle is probably

00:10:57.964 --> 00:10:59.356
one of our signature dishes.

00:10:59.356 --> 00:11:01.179
It's basically a play on
chicken waffles if you will.

00:11:01.179 --> 00:11:02.617
The batter is Yukon gold potatoes,

00:11:02.617 --> 00:11:04.326
a little bit of flour, some magic,

00:11:04.326 --> 00:11:05.382
some love, and buttermilk.

00:11:05.382 --> 00:11:07.043
And then on top we do very acidic bernese.

00:11:07.043 --> 00:11:08.504
I think a lot of bernese are very muted

00:11:08.504 --> 00:11:09.806
and the just become very fatty.

00:11:09.806 --> 00:11:11.217
But you have this rich potato waffle.

00:11:11.217 --> 00:11:12.824
You have lobster that's very light.

00:11:12.824 --> 00:11:14.496
And then we just want to air
it out with everything else.

00:11:14.496 --> 00:11:15.936
There's an art to eating a buffet.

00:11:15.936 --> 00:11:17.814
You always want more
than what you can finish.

00:11:17.814 --> 00:11:20.464
If you leave fat and happy, I'm happy.

00:11:20.464 --> 00:11:21.369
(laughing)
That's the whole point.

00:11:21.369 --> 00:11:23.018
- [Steven] So, there will
be plenty of food for Adam.

00:11:23.018 --> 00:11:24.097
- [David] There will be
plenty of food for Adam.

00:11:24.097 --> 00:11:25.224
- [Andrew] I think we're ready to do it.

00:11:25.224 --> 00:11:26.127
- [David] Great.

00:11:26.127 --> 00:11:26.960
Crush it.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:27.793
Crush brunch.

00:11:27.793 --> 00:11:28.626
- [Andrew] Crush brunch isn't a phrase

00:11:28.626 --> 00:11:30.425
that I expect coming out
of a place like this.

00:11:30.425 --> 00:11:31.283
- [David] Free flowing.

00:11:31.283 --> 00:11:32.116
Crush it.

00:11:32.116 --> 00:11:32.949
- [Andrew] Free flowing.

00:11:32.949 --> 00:11:33.782
Crush it.

00:11:33.782 --> 00:11:36.532
Thanks for dressing up, for once.

00:11:37.666 --> 00:11:39.489
Ooh, that's (beep) smooth.

00:11:39.489 --> 00:11:40.703
- We need to crush this brunch.

00:11:40.703 --> 00:11:42.017
So I think we need a game plan here.

00:11:42.017 --> 00:11:43.283
I think we should--
- Maybe we should cheers the--

00:11:43.283 --> 00:11:47.033
- Maybe uh, the lamb.
- No the waffle lobster.

00:11:48.832 --> 00:11:50.456
- You want to lead with
the waffle lobster.

00:11:50.456 --> 00:11:53.300
- Yeah, it's one of the
few things we can pick up.

00:11:53.300 --> 00:11:54.133
- Cheers.

00:11:56.864 --> 00:11:58.849
- Mmm.
- Oh yeah.

00:11:58.849 --> 00:12:01.078
- There's like chunks
of potato in the waffle.

00:12:01.078 --> 00:12:03.062
There's this delightful cream on top.

00:12:03.062 --> 00:12:04.515
- Chicken and waffles,
you think you've reached

00:12:04.515 --> 00:12:06.684
the pinnacle of life when you try that.

00:12:06.684 --> 00:12:07.517
Mm mm.

00:12:07.517 --> 00:12:08.950
- Lobster and waffles, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:11.527
- Look how fat and juicy this shrimp is.

00:12:11.527 --> 00:12:12.849
I don't think I've ever had a shrimp

00:12:12.849 --> 00:12:15.300
that fat and juicy in my life.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.646
- Mmm, want somebody to stop talking?

00:12:17.646 --> 00:12:19.480
- Holy (beep).
- Feed them this shrimp.

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:20.313
Because it fills your mouth.

00:12:20.313 --> 00:12:22.162
- Yeah, cop a shrimp in their mouth.

00:12:22.162 --> 00:12:24.542
- While on the same theme here, come on!

00:12:24.542 --> 00:12:27.125
- Come on.
- This is next level!

00:12:28.859 --> 00:12:30.556
- Oh yeah.
- Mmm.

00:12:30.556 --> 00:12:31.462
(slurps and coughs)

00:12:31.462 --> 00:12:33.697
- (laughs) Easy there big fella.

00:12:33.697 --> 00:12:35.430
- Just trying to crush this brunch.

00:12:35.430 --> 00:12:37.097
- Let's do the lamb.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:38.953
- Cheers.

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:43.435
No joke, wow!
- Holy (beep) that's crazy.

00:12:43.435 --> 00:12:46.141
- That lamb is so tender to bite into.

00:12:46.141 --> 00:12:47.698
- You know what the best part of bunch is?

00:12:47.698 --> 00:12:49.568
You get delicious seafood,

00:12:49.568 --> 00:12:51.251
the best of breakfast--
- Mm hmm

00:12:51.251 --> 00:12:52.876
- You get a beautifully carved lamb.

00:12:52.876 --> 00:12:53.889
And then if you want to,

00:12:53.889 --> 00:12:57.500
you just have a donut right after that.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:58.382
This is a really good donut.

00:12:58.382 --> 00:12:59.890
(laughing) Everything's really good.

00:12:59.890 --> 00:13:01.494
- Can I have some?

00:13:01.494 --> 00:13:02.327
Ah man!

00:13:03.444 --> 00:13:06.358
- What'd you expect?
- Oh!

00:13:06.358 --> 00:13:09.446
- (laughing) Yeah!

00:13:09.446 --> 00:13:11.442
It's a really good donut.

00:13:11.442 --> 00:13:13.220
(laughing)

00:13:13.220 --> 00:13:14.767
- That was like biting into cream cheese.

00:13:14.767 --> 00:13:15.962
- Is that the pork belly?
- No, no

00:13:15.962 --> 00:13:17.693
- I didn't, I actually
didn't get pork belly.

00:13:17.693 --> 00:13:21.193
- Uh oh.
(classical music)

00:13:23.045 --> 00:13:24.990
Wow.
- That was so soft.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.488
It's like mashed potatoes.

00:13:26.488 --> 00:13:27.765
It's like pig Jello.

00:13:27.765 --> 00:13:28.775
- You know I dream about that.

00:13:28.775 --> 00:13:30.982
- Pig Jello?
- Yes.

00:13:30.982 --> 00:13:33.756
- (exhales) Thank you.
- Oh, uh.

00:13:33.756 --> 00:13:35.657
- Top off?
- You're here, yeah, why not?

00:13:35.657 --> 00:13:37.896
Brunch is when you wanna
become a Greek god.

00:13:37.896 --> 00:13:40.055
Feeding yourself, like grapes, like this.

00:13:40.055 --> 00:13:42.273
- Mm hmm.
- Shoving donuts?

00:13:42.273 --> 00:13:43.167
- I think more than anything else

00:13:43.167 --> 00:13:45.987
brunch is about taking your time to eat

00:13:45.987 --> 00:13:47.068
just, whatever you want.

00:13:47.068 --> 00:13:48.530
I kinda get it now.
- You feel it?

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:49.363
Do you feel the love?

00:13:49.363 --> 00:13:50.328
The good times?

00:13:50.328 --> 00:13:51.851
The memories that you'll never forget?

00:13:51.851 --> 00:13:52.907
- Uh, yeah.

00:13:52.907 --> 00:13:53.941
(laughing) I love brunch.

00:13:53.941 --> 00:13:56.191
(laughing)

00:14:03.498 --> 00:14:04.661
- Were you wearing a belt earlier?

00:14:04.661 --> 00:14:05.603
- Yeah, I had to take it off

00:14:05.603 --> 00:14:08.099
because of the uh, constriction.

00:14:08.099 --> 00:14:10.177
- Alright Andrew, which brunch

00:14:10.177 --> 00:14:12.510
was the most worth it at its price to you?

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:15.297
- My favorite brunch spot was HomeState.

00:14:15.297 --> 00:14:17.938
Because, if you want a low impact brunch,

00:14:17.938 --> 00:14:18.890
you can have it there.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:20.222
And if you want to ball hard

00:14:20.222 --> 00:14:22.511
and dip your breakfast taco into

00:14:22.511 --> 00:14:25.020
a cheese pool, you can do that too.

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:25.853
Actually, no.

00:14:25.853 --> 00:14:26.831
A-Frame is my Worth It winner.

00:14:26.831 --> 00:14:27.664
- What?
- Sorry.

00:14:27.664 --> 00:14:28.497
Uh, no.

00:14:28.497 --> 00:14:30.143
HomeState is my Worth It winner.

00:14:30.143 --> 00:14:32.117
- (laughing) No, you
can't, you can't go one way

00:14:32.117 --> 00:14:34.358
and then go the other way
and then go the other way.

00:14:34.358 --> 00:14:36.517
- The problem is that
breakfast tacos are such

00:14:36.517 --> 00:14:38.363
a good savory breakfast food,

00:14:38.363 --> 00:14:40.418
and pancakes are such a good sweet.

00:14:40.418 --> 00:14:41.997
It's really hard to choose between them.

00:14:41.997 --> 00:14:43.888
- I gotta say, my worth it winner,

00:14:43.888 --> 00:14:44.967
I mean, you know who I'm gonna pick.

00:14:44.967 --> 00:14:45.800
A-Frame.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:47.542
That macadamia nut pancake.

00:14:47.542 --> 00:14:50.131
Oh my gosh, I'm still dreaming about it.

00:14:50.131 --> 00:14:51.131
Adam?
- Adam?

00:14:52.291 --> 00:14:54.044
- I win.
- You don't win.

00:14:54.044 --> 00:14:55.275
- This is the first time on this show

00:14:55.275 --> 00:14:56.958
he picked something with me.

00:14:56.958 --> 00:14:58.177
Shout out to Belvedere though.

00:14:58.177 --> 00:15:00.186
- It was great.
- Seafood lovers out there,

00:15:00.186 --> 00:15:01.091
That's your spot.

00:15:01.091 --> 00:15:05.027
Next time you see us we might be in Japan.

00:15:05.027 --> 00:15:07.277
(laughing)

00:15:10.655 --> 00:15:12.244
- [Andrew] Cut the tape.

00:15:12.244 --> 00:15:14.584
- [Steven] Sorry to the editors, oh yes!

